# NOTE: requirements-prod.txt is no longer generated from this file.
#
# Do not run `pip-compile requirements-prod.in` -- it would overwrite
# requirements-prod.txt with a freshly resolved lockfile and undo the reason that
# file exists. Two independent compiled lockfiles drifted apart once already and
# the divergence went unnoticed for as long as the Docker build stayed broken;
# the full account is in the header of requirements-prod.txt.
#
# requirements-prod.txt now reads `-r requirements.txt` and adds the handful of
# server-only packages by hand. Edit it directly.
#
# This file is kept only to record what production asks for on top of the
# library's own requirements.

# Base requirements
-r requirements.in

# Production-only dependencies
gunicorn
uvicorn[standard]
